## VI. WHAT I COULD NOT REACH

`WebSearch` (exhausted before start) and every general search engine (CAPTCHA). **OpenAlex hit its daily budget mid-session for four of seven investigations.** arXiv returned empty under our own parallel load in one lane. **The Internet Archive was offline all session** — which is why instance mortality could not be reconstructed. Hard-blocked hosts: Reddit, Ars Technica, Wired, Verge, Guardian, BBC, Reuters, AP, Washington Post, ACM DL PDFs, IEEE, Science/Cell paywalls, `ftc.gov/system/files/`, `ico.org.uk`, `federalregister.gov`, `erights.org` (connection refused), `biscuitsec.org`, `usenix.org` via WebFetch, and — late in the session — **`support.google.com`, which CAPTCHA'd our egress**, so all Google evidence above is via Wayback with snapshot timestamps.

Specifically unretrieved, and **not** filled from memory: Karst et al.'s internal N and citation-bias percentages; Whiteside 2019's fold-differences; Kiers 2011 full text; Matthews et al. CHI 2016's numbers; Ghosh "A Matter of Control or Safety?" effect sizes; Brennan/Afroz/Greenstadt adversarial-stylometry figures (6 mirrors tried); Clark's 1988 DARPA design-philosophy goal ordering; the CSRB Storm-0558 PDF (403 from three government hosts — **the "60,000 State Department emails" and "paused key rotation" figures are therefore UNVERIFIED, do not attribute them to the CSRB**); Microsoft's own Sept-2023 Storm-0558 post-mortem (301'd away); Schomp et al. IMC 2013; McDaniel & Rubin's rebuttal to Rivest — *the most directly adversarial source to the expiry thesis, reached as metadata only*; n0's actual hole-punching publication (the two cited URLs do not exist among n0's 82 blog slugs — only *"roughly 90% of network conditions"*, undated and method-free, and a 95%-of-*bytes* figure); Tor sponsor amounts (never disclosed, any sponsor, any year); measured offboarding/deprovisioning latency (nothing in Crossref or HN — treat any figure as vendor-survey grade); s.76 offence statistics for 2020/21–2025/26 (ONS does not disaggregate CCB); Apple's Secure Enclave partitioning per Shared iPad user (**the security page never mentions SEP**); and the final outcome of the LFGSS shutdown.

**One operational note:** the `lares` MCP server failed to connect this whole session (CONNECTION_CLOSED) — it played no part in this research, and two of my agents flagged it independently. Worth a retry before the next pass.
